Day 11: Leap Year Checker

Concepts used:
 input(),
 int(),
 modulo %,
 logical operators (and, or)


Problem Statement

Write a Python program that:

1.Asks the user to enter a year.
2.Checks whether it's a leap year using these rules:
     i) Divisible by 4 AND not divisible by 100 → leap year
    ii) OR divisible by 400 → leap year
   iii) Otherwise → not a leap year
3.Prints the result.


Example Run
Enter a year: 2024
2024 is a leap year.

Enter a year: 1900
1900 is NOT a leap year.

Enter a year: 2000
2000 is a leap year.

Hint
if (year % 4 == 0 and year % 100 != 0) or (year % 400 == 0):  # leap year

Try to understand why each part of this condition is needed — think about why 1900 is not a leap year but 2000 is, even though both are divisible by 100.


Bonus (optional)
Loop so the user can check multiple years until they type q to quit.
